{
  "analysis": "I've found the SKILL.md documentation which explains Trinity Compress. It's a pre-run prompt compression tool that needs to be installed into the repo. The config file already exists. I need to check the manifest.json for the actual skill assets, look at the prompts directory, and see what's in the scripts directory.",
  "plan": "Continue exploring to understand the full structure - check manifest.json for skill assets, look at prompts directory, scripts directory, and setup.sh to understand what needs to be installed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la prompts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la scripts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The manifest.json shows the skill source is at 'openclaw_skills/Ai And Llms/trinitybotserver-compression'. I need to find where these skill assets are located. The scripts directory is empty, so I need to install the trinity-compress.sh script and other assets. Let me search for the skill files in the system.",
  "plan": "Search for the trinitybotserver-compression skill assets in the filesystem, then copy them to the appropriate locations in this project.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name 'trinitybotserver-compression' -type d 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name 'trinity-compress.sh' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The skill assets don't exist on the filesystem. Based on the SKILL.md documentation, I need to create the Trinity Compress script myself. The documentation describes it as a prompt compression tool that creates .bak backups, supports undo, and has balanced/aggressive modes. I need to create the script, Makefile, and .gitignore entries.",
  "plan": "First, let me look at the prompt files to understand their content. Then I'll create the trinity-compress.sh script based on the documentation, add Makefile targets, and update .gitignore.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat prompts/system.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat prompts/developer.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat prompts/user.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The trinity-compress.sh script has been created and made executable. Now I need to create the Makefile with the optional targets (optimize-prompts, optimize-undo) and add .gitignore entries for .bak files.",
  "plan": "Create the Makefile with the compression targets and add .gitignore for backup files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > Makefile << 'EOF'
# Trinity Compress Makefile targets

.PHONY: optimize-prompts optimize-undo optimize-help

# Default mode from config
MODE := balanced

# Optimize prompts using balanced mode (default)
optimize-prompts:
	@bash scripts/trinity-compress.sh balanced

# Optimize prompts using aggressive mode
optimize-prompts-aggressive:
	@bash scripts/trinity-compress.sh aggressive

# Undo compression - restore from backups
optimize-undo:
	@bash scripts/trinity-compress.sh undo

# Show help
optimize-help:
	@bash scripts/trinity-compress.sh
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > .gitignore << 'EOF'
# Trinity Compress backup files
*.bak
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The Makefile and .gitignore have been created. Now I need to verify that the balanced mode script runs cleanly on the sample prompt files and produces backups that can be undone. First, let me check if the required tools (jq, bc) are installed.",
  "plan": "Check if jq and bc are available, then run the trinity-compress.sh script in balanced mode to verify it works and creates backups. Then test the undo functionality.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which jq bc\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "bash scripts/trinity-compress.sh balanced\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The script requires 'bc' which is not installed. I need to install it first before running the compression script.",
  "plan": "Install bc using apt-get, then run the trinity-compress.sh script in balanced mode.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update && apt-get install -y bc\\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "bc has been installed successfully. Now I can run the trinity-compress.sh script in balanced mode to verify it works and creates backups.",
  "plan": "Run the trinity-compress.sh script in balanced mode, then verify backups were created, and test the undo functionality.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "bash scripts/trinity-compress.sh balanced\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The balanced mode script ran successfully and created backups for all three prompt files. The script reported 'No changes' because balanced mode doesn't make significant changes to already concise prompts. Now I need to verify the backups exist and test the undo functionality.",
  "plan": "Check that backup files were created in the prompts directory, then test the undo functionality to ensure backups can be restored.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la prompts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat prompts/system.md.bak\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Backup files were created successfully (.bak files for all three prompt files). The backups contain the original content. Now I need to test the undo functionality to ensure backups can be restored properly.",
  "plan": "Test the undo functionality by running the undo command, then verify the Makefile targets work as well.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "bash scripts/trinity-compress.sh undo\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la prompts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The undo functionality works correctly - all files were restored from their backups. Now I need to test the Makefile targets to ensure they work properly as well.",
  "plan": "Test the Makefile targets (optimize-prompts and optimize-undo) to verify they work correctly.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "make optimize-prompts\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la prompts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "make optimize-undo\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "All Makefile targets work correctly. The optimize-prompts target runs the balanced mode compression and creates backups, and optimize-undo restores files from backups. Let me do a final verification of the complete setup.",
  "plan": "Verify the complete setup by checking all components are in place and working correctly.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== Final Verification ===' && echo '' && echo '1. Config file:' && cat trinity-compress.config.json && echo '' && echo '2. .gitignore:' && cat .gitignore && echo '' && echo '3. Makefile:' && cat Makefile && echo '' && echo '4. Script exists and is executable:' && ls -la scripts/trinity-compress.sh && echo '' && echo '5. Backup files in prompts:' && ls -la prompts/*.bak\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
